    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Gene’s debut album Olympian is a polished Britpop record that blends chiming guitar pop, melodic urgency, and a distinctly melancholic emotional tone. Released in 1995 on Costermonger, it helped establish the band as one of the era’s more literate and introspective acts, with songs that balance anthemic choruses against self-doubt, romantic tension, and social unease. The album peaked at No. 8 in the UK and earned strong reviews, later coming to be regarded as one of the standout debuts of the decade.\n\nWhat gives Olympian its staying power is the way it tempers classic indie-rock influences with a more vulnerable, hopeful sensibility. Tracks such as “Haunted by You,” “Still Can’t Find the Phone,” and the title song became key singles, while the album’s reputation grew beyond its initial Britpop moment thanks to its emotional depth and careful songwriting. It remains a defining statement from Gene: stylish, heartfelt, and more enduring than many of its flashier contemporaries.",
